<section id="privacy">
  <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: August 26, 2026</p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information Flame ("the Bot") collects, how we use it, and what rights you have over it.</p>

  <h3>1. Information we collect</h3>
  <p>Depending on the OAuth2 permissions (scopes) you explicitly authorize, Flame may collect and store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Discord identifiers:</strong> your user ID, username, avatar, and the servers you share with the Bot (<code>identify</code>, <code>guilds</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Email address:</strong> if you authorize the <code>email</code> scope, we may store the email address associated with your Discord account.</li>
    <li><strong>Voice connection data:</strong> if the Bot offers voice features, it may process technical connection metadata (for example, which voice channel you join), but it does not record or store audio unless explicitly stated for a specific feature.</li>
    <li><strong>Server data:</strong> settings, roles, channels, and configurations that administrators set up for the Bot to function.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> only if a specific Bot feature requires it (for example, moderation or commands), and only the content necessary to execute that feature.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect data that is not tied to the OAuth2 scopes you approve or to the Bot's normal functions within Discord.</p>

  <h3>2. How we use your information</h3>
  <p>We use the collected data only to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide and maintain the Bot's features.</li>
    <li>Personalize your experience within the servers where Flame is present.</li>
    <li>Detect and prevent abuse, fraud, or activity that violates our Terms of Service.</li>
    <li>Improve the Bot's performance and functionality.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. We do not sell your data</h3>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for advertising or commercial purposes.</p>

  <h3>4. Data sharing</h3>
  <p>We may share information only in these cases:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>With infrastructure providers (for example, hosting or databases) strictly necessary to operate the Bot.</li>
    <li>If required by law under a valid legal request.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5. Data retention and deletion</h3>
  <p>We retain data only for as long as necessary for the Bot to function or while the server/user keeps the Bot installed. You may request deletion of your data at any time by contacting us through our support server; we will process the request within a reasonable timeframe.</p>

  <h3>6. Security</h3>
  <p>We apply reasonable measures to protect stored information, although no system is 100% secure. We work to minimize the risk of unauthorized access.</p>

  <h3>7. Children's privacy</h3>
  <p>Flame is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age required by Discord in your country). If we discover we have collected data from a minor without appropriate authorization, we will delete it.</p>

  <h3>8. Changes to this Policy</h3>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. We will notify significant changes by updating the "Last updated" date on this document.</p>

